11. LIQUIDATED DAMAGES

11.1 In lieu of proving actual damages for unauthorized use of the
Software, Licensee agrees to pay liquidated damages as follows:
(a) for unauthorized access or study: ten thousand US dollars
(USD 10,000) per instance; (b) for unauthorized use in a Competing
Product: fifty thousand US dollars (USD 50,000) per instance plus
twenty percent (20%) of Licensee's gross revenue attributable to the
Competing Product for the period of unauthorized use; (c) for
unauthorized disclosure: twenty-five thousand US dollars (USD 25,000)
per disclosure.

11.2 Each instance of unauthorized use constitutes a separate
violation. Continuing violations accrue daily.

11.3 These liquidated damages represent a genuine pre-estimate of
harm and not a penalty. The parties agree that actual damages would
be difficult or impossible to calculate and that these amounts are
reasonable in light of the anticipated or actual harm.

11.4 If any court determines that the liquidated damages in this
section constitute a penalty, the parties agree that the court may
reduce the amount to the maximum enforceable amount, and the remaining
provisions of this License shall continue in full force.

